message: "If you use this software or repository in your research, please cite the associated work."
type: software
title: "Self-Supervised Multi-Layer Vision Transformer Representations for Industrial Anomaly Detection and Localization"
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mohsinfaridd/ViT_Anomaly_Detection_SimCLR"
authors:
  - family-names: "Farid"
    given-names: "Mohsin"
  - family-names: "Raza"
    given-names: "Muhammad Asif"
  - family-names: "Ziani"
    given-names: "Abdelhakim"
  - family-names: "Rashid"
    given-names: "Muhammad"
abstract: >-
  This repository provides the implementation, reproducibility code,
  evaluation notebooks, figure-generation scripts, and analysis utilities for a
  self-supervised Vision Transformer study of industrial anomaly detection and
  localization on MVTec AD. Protocol A performs category-conditioned binary
  normal-versus-anomaly detection with known category identity at inference,
  using multi-layer ViT patch representations, normal prototype memories,
  normal-only calibration, and raw patch-distance localization.
keywords:
  - industrial anomaly detection
  - anomaly localization
  - Vision Transformer
  - ViT
  - self-supervised learning
  - SimCLR
  - MVTec AD
  - computer vision
  - industrial inspection
  - reproducibility
